    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When a frontier plant failure point triggered a technical failure event, the energy system operator was pushed to the edge of grid stability. Officials, acting as crisis decision-makers, ordered an emergency measure to prevent a power shortage from spiraling. This load reduction measure, a bold intervention to save the grid, kept a critical transmission line from overloading, but the resulting generation capacity shortfall highlighted the fragility of the system under heatwave impact.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The Visayas region, an alert zone at the edge, faced a massive power frontier closure after a system breach at the boundary. Chronic infrastructure limits and thermal-driven load strain pushed the grid into a high demand crisis. In response, authority figures implemented a load shedding control action, a reactive caging of demand to stabilize the grid, exposing the underlying power outage and capacity loss across the island group.",
